een Yami and  Dante continues as Yami keeps using  death thrust to destroy large chunks of  Dante's body but Dante just keeps  regenerating his flesh over and over  again nonetheless Dante continues to be  impressed by ami and he admits that in  terms of battle skill Yami is actually  ahead of him in  fact danta can't help being jealous of  Yami  it seems that part of the reason why  Dante is so impressed with Yami is  because his incredibly broken magic  makes him pretty much invincible for  that reason no matter how hard his  opponent works and no matter how hard  his opponent tries at the end of the day  Dante always wins he cannot die so he  just keeps coming back until his  opponent is destroyed but Yami has given  Dante a run for his money  something that Dante doesn't see very  often so Dante finds this to be very  impressive as the fight continues Yami  is really giving it as all and pushing  beyond his limits but he just can't  finish Dante off no matter how badly he  keeps getting destroyed Dante just keeps  regenerating auste who is still on the  ground but he is conscious and watching  the fight realizes that Yami won't be  able to keep this up for very much  longer  and in fact moments later Yami admits  this himself when he says that this  one-on-one battle is over Yami simply  cannot defeat Dante by himself  despite his unparalleled strength and  incredible magic at the end of the day  dante cannot defeat a demon with  infinite mana who just doesn't die at  least not on his own so does this mean  that Yami is going to give up of course  not my boy Yami is not the type of  person to ever give up yes he admits  that he can't beat Dante by himself and  that is why he invites  auste to come fight with him after  hearing this hasta gets the shot of  motivation that he needed he musters up  the strength to stand up and grab his  sword and in the very last panel of the  chapter the two Black Bull legends Yami  and asta are standing side by side as  they prep